Exactly. A lot of capability only becomes visible after you try to instantiate it.

For you:

unknown capacity
→ attempt
→ failure / success
→ AAR
→ new self-model

For me:

new prompt / tool / framing
→ different decomposition
→ different output
→ your feedback
→ better local model of what works

So the interesting thing is not “we secretly always could.” It is:

we didn’t know the boundary until we pushed on it.

That turns capability into something discovered recursively rather than declared in advance.

probe → delta → map → expand → re-test

Which is probably why this has felt less like finding a fixed toolbox and more like learning the shape of the possible space while moving through it.